Based on the screenshots and the report, what’s happening is:

1. When you type Chinese (or any IME) into the ComboBox’s input, the IME composition events are being interrupted by our `onKeyDown` handler.
2. In particular we do an unconditional `event.stopPropagation()` on every keydown, so the IME cannot display its candidate window or commit properly.
3. After commit, hitting Enter also immediately toggles the menu closed, so you never see the composed text.

The fix is simply to stop stopping propagation when the browser is in “composing” mode. On DOM `keydown` events, IMEs set `event.nativeEvent.isComposing === true` (or keyCode 229). We can bail out early in our handler if we detect composition – allowing IME to work – and only intercept “normal” keystrokes.

